    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d840">

                <pb facs="0916" n="1750" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/412</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commercial Adviser of the British Embassy</hi>
                        (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crawford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Assistant to the Counselor for the Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Auchincloss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Auchincloss</hi>: We have received a telegram from the
                    Foreign Office to the effect that the British authorities concur in the
                    recognition of the transfer of flag in the case of the three Chilean ships, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Karnak, Alda</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Göttingen</hi> on the understanding that the vessels will carry no crew,
                    officers or passengers of enemy nationality and that they will transport
                    nitrates to the United States.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office also add that they thoroughly agree with your proposal for
                    mutual consultation between our two Governments before giving any definite reply
                    in the event of applications being <pb facs="0917" n="1751" xml:id="pg1751"/>
                    made by South American Governments in the future for transfer of flag.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. S. Hudson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/> (In the absence of Sir R.
                        Crawford)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
